  bx('pk', "<b>Board: no political control (no colonialism or imperialism) = trade was good for India.</b> [1757: colonialism began; Goa an exception.] Europeans came to buy Indian <b>FINISHED GOODS</b>; competition among Europeans and between Arabs and Europeans. Good for: exports, forex, strength of Indian kingdoms, <b>better price</b>, Indian merchants, Indian artisans."),
  fl(["Ryots + artisans (villages) produce", "Indian merchant (town): domestic trade", "Coast: Arabs / Europeans meet: international trade", "Europeans pay export duty to the Indian ruler", "OUT OF INDIA"], "Flow of goods (teacher's board)", 5),
  t("<b>Europe not wealthy: spices, 800%</b>", "Eastern goods = luxuries for the rich only; Genoa + Venice guarded the position", "Until the <b>1600s</b> European food as spiced as Indian: clove + pepper preserved winter meat (no refrigerator)", "<b>Da Gama's 1498 cargo = 800% profit</b>; by 1600s <b>1 kg clove = 1 kg gold</b>", "Board: <b>6 months</b> = journey EU to India; Indonesia wanted nothing from EU; buyer pays Gold/Silver = depletes forex; side note [Savings Bank A/c: 4% 6-7%]", "Handout hook: in the 1650s children would be &quot;spitting gold&quot; (clove in rice) = <b>clove = gold</b>", w=22),
