  t("<b>Why trade, not empire?</b>", "Primary purpose = <b>trade</b>. Empire building happened in the Americas (<b>weak states</b>); India had <b>strong land powers</b>", "Gains of empire: mining resources (gold, silver), greater trade profits, land revenue + taxes, export to home at a low price", "South India vulnerable: <b>no Mughal Empire yet (1526-1858)</b>; split between <b>Vijayanagara (1336-1646)</b> + Deccan Sultanates, no unified naval power (south weak since <b>Talikota 1565</b>)", "Portuguese = part <b>commerce</b>, part <b>conquest</b>, part <b>coercion</b>", w=22),
  bx('bl', "<b>West coast north to south (board):</b> Diu, Surat, Daman, Bombay, Goa, Mahe, Calicut, Cochin, Travancore (+ Broach/Bharuch). Calicut and Cochin = small kingdoms (Cochin on Travancore's northern border). <b>Map dates:</b> Diu 1535 P, Surat 1612 British, Daman 1558 P, Bassein 1533 P, Bombay 1638 B, Goa 1610 P, Cannanore 1501 P, Mahe 1725 French, Calicut 1498 P, Cochin 1500 P (Dutch 1669), Colombo 1505 P (Dutch 1656)."),
