  t("<b>Francisco de Almeida 05-09</b>", "<b>1st Governor</b> of the Estado da India (legal title <b>Governador</b>, commonly Viceroy); board: CEO in India; from 1510+ Governor = CEO + CM of Goa", "<b>Blue Water Policy</b> = naval supremacy over oceans/trade routes, not territorial conquest; goal = monopolistic trading regime; <b>Goa 1510 = the exception</b>", "<b>Why:</b> better navy goal = oceanic trade; Indian armies strong; Europe's navy usually greater (exceptions Marathas, Travancore). Land-only states = territorial army; coastal states = army + navy (Portugal, Dutch, French, British, Spain)", t("<b>Cartaz</b>", "Naval pass all non-Portuguese ships must buy to sail safely in the Indian Ocean", "<b>Toll booth on the sea</b>"), w=22),
  t("<b>Battle of Diu 1509</b>", "A fight for <b>domination of the Arabian Sea</b>, not Diu as territory", "Coalition of the old routes' stakeholders: <b>Arabs (Egypt, Mamluks), Gujarat, Zamorin</b>, backed by <b>Ottoman</b> ships and <b>Venice</b>; Portugal won", "1502 Arabs + Zamorin beaten; 1509 top player of the Arabian Sea; Venice's trade being destroyed", "Only under <b>Akbar 56-05</b> was the coastal area added to the Mughal state", w=22),
  sec("ALBUQUERQUE 09-15 AND NUNO DA CUNHA 29-38", 'r'),
