  t("<b>Albuquerque 09-15</b> (2nd Governor, 1509-15)", "Arrived (back in India 1508) with King's orders; <b>Almeida 05-09 distrusted and arrested him</b>; after Diu 1509 new fleet confirmed orders, released, 2nd Governor (title Governador, not Viceroy)", "<b>Territorial transformation: annexed Goa 1510 from the Sultan of Bijapur</b> (Babur 26-30 not in India in 1510): trade enterprise became territorial colonial State", "<b>Luso-Indian policy</b>: intermarriage with Indian women (many war widows or captured, often forced) = bigger Portuguese population, stability (like Mughal more mansabdars = co-opted)", "Co-opted local elites into administration; attempted to regulate <b>Sati</b>; promoted Christianity as tool of political control", w=24),
  bx('pk', "<b>Board:</b> two ways to power: (1) fight, defeat, remove all (2) <b>co-opt</b> (e.g. Babur 26-30, Akbar 56-05). <b>Religion = soft power:</b> conversion reduces opposition, narrative of brotherhood; social power raises political power. <b>Abolition of Sati (any reform) has two intents:</b> (1) conversion, by weakening bond with religion / mocking rituals (2) noble: reform, women's empowerment."),
  t("<b>Nuno da Cunha 29-38</b> (Governor 1529-38) = peak", "<b>1530</b> HQ shifted Cochin to <b>Goa</b>; dominated Indian Ocean trade ~a century", "<b>Bassein 1534</b> and <b>Diu 1535</b> from <b>Bahadur Shah of Gujarat</b>", "Board: 1613 EIC's Surat factory, after defeating Portuguese, ends the &quot;nearly a century&quot;; &quot;+ BOMBAY (1534)&quot;, permission of the Sultan of Gujarat", w=20),
