  t("<b>1588 Armada</b>", "<b>Britain + Dutch Republic</b> (Netherlands = Holland = Dutch Republic) emerged 2nd half of 16th C; wanted <b>freedom of navigation</b> in oceans and trade", "<b>1588 British Navy beat Spanish Armada</b> in the Atlantic; <b>by 1580 Portugal in union with Spain</b>, so Portuguese routes opened too; safe to Asia via CoGH", "<b>First priority Indonesia</b> (spice islands); India later: islanders wanted <b>Indian cotton</b>, so cloth from India first = <b>triangle: England (EIC) to India to Indonesia to England (EIC)</b>", w=22),
  t("<b>Board: monopoly must be broken</b>", "End rival's monopoly (e.g. 1502 Da Gama in Malabar) leads to multi-player domain, then own monopoly (needs more resources: Diu 1509 Arabian Sea)", "<b>2 challenges</b> for British + Dutch: (1) reach India, China, Indonesia (Spain + Portugal hold routes) (2) buy goods in India (Portuguese hold coast + market). 1588 = end of monopoly over routes", w=20),
  tb(["Period", "Dominant oceanic trade power"], ["1500s", "Portugal vs Spain"], ["1600s", "Dutch vs British"], ["1700s-1815", "British vs French: <b>Britain top naval power</b>"], ["1870-1945", "British + French vs Germany"], ["1945-91", "US vs USSR"], ["2000s+", "US vs China"]),
  bx('bl', "<b>CHARTER</b> = founding document issued by the State (Monarchy or Parliament) granting special powers and rights to a company. <b>State</b> = territorial motive (defend, annex), military, may wage war, coins + currency + taxation + L-E-J powers. <b>Company</b> = profit motive for shareholders, requires property."),
  sec("THE DUTCH VOC", 'b'),
  stl(7, 'Because the VOC had capital and a Charter, it beat the Portuguese in the south.'),
  t("<b>VOC 1602</b> " + P('2022'), "<b>Vereenigde Oost-Indische Compagnie</b>, Charter of the <b>Dutch Parliament</b>, <b>merged six</b> smaller companies", "<b>World's first multinational</b> and first to issue <b>publicly tradable stocks on a formal exchange = first joint-stock company</b> (ancestor of BSE, NSE, NYSE); shareholders no say in management", "<b>Charter powers: war, treaties, territory, forts, own currency</b>; board: big company = deep pockets = more buying power (merger + joint stock)", "<b>1st Dutch expedition 1595</b> went to East Indies, not India", "<b>Peak 1669</b>: richest private company: 150 merchant vessels, 40 warships, army 10,000, 50,000 employees; <b>5,000 voyages</b>", "<b>1799</b> taken over by Dutch govt = Dutch East Indies (Indonesia), colony till <b>1945</b>; fell: bankrupt (English EIC competition) + defeats in French Revolutionary Wars 1792-1804 + Napoleonic War 1804-15", w=24),
  bx('ye', "<b>Prelims 2022 trap:</b> the claim that the Dutch got land from the <b>Gajapati</b> dynasty (15th C Odisha, declined long before) is INCORRECT. Do not confuse later Odisha-coast rulers with the Gajapatis."),
  tl(("1605", "<b>Masulipatnam</b> (Northern Sarkars): first Dutch factory in India"), ("1610", "<b>Pulicat</b> (Carnatic, Vijayanagara zone): Fort Geldria, first Dutch fort, main HQ 1610-90"), ("1616", "Surat (Gujarat)"), ("1641", "Bimilipatam (Golconda)"), ("1645", "Karikal"), ("1653", "<b>Chinsura</b> (Bengal), Fort Gustavus"), ("1663", "<b>Cochin</b>: captured from Portuguese, HQ of Dutch <b>Malabar</b> only"), ("1690", "Main HQ moves to <b>Nagapattinam</b> (to 1795)")),
  bx('bl', "Also later: Kasimbazar, Baranagore, Patna, Balasore, Nagapatnam, Agra, Cochin. Board: Masulipatnam lay in the Northern Sarkars under Golconda (Golconda 1687 annexed by Aurangzeb 58-07); N. Sarkars (5 districts, number partly legible). <b>HQ example:</b> Amazon India HQ Bengaluru, regional HQ Gurgaon: Pulicat then Nagapattinam = main HQ; Cochin = regional only."),
  bx('ye', "<b>Source conflicts:</b> handout dates Fort Gustavus (Chinsura) 1655-1795, section 6 and Table T2 give the Chinsura factory 1653. <b>Trap: Cochin was NOT the overall Dutch HQ.</b> Board: 1605 Portuguese Cochin factory 1500 stays the first European factory."),
  sec("THE ENGLISH EIC AND THE CHARTER OF 1600", 'r'),
  stl(8, 'Because the EIC lived on a licence, its Charter shaped its fate.'),
  t("<b>EIC 1600</b>", "Formed <b>31 Dec 1600</b>: <b>Royal Charter of Elizabeth I 58-03</b> = a licence from the Monarch; not renewed = company ceases; survival depends on goodwill of power in Britain", "<b>4th joint-stock company in England</b>; pooled money of <b>215 London merchants</b> (merchant adventurers) to challenge Dutch dominance; goal = trade with the East, not empire", "In 1600 it was <b>England</b>, not Britain: England + Scotland united <b>1707</b> (Great Britain); Ireland added <b>1801</b> (UK)", w=22),
  t("<b>The Charter gave 3 things</b>", "<b>Monopoly over England's trade with the East Indies for 15 years</b> (WRONG: monopoly over trade with India)", "<b>Right to carry gold (forex) out of England</b>: forex controlled by the State", "<b>Private management</b>: Governor, Deputy Governor + 24 members = later <b>Board / Court of Directors</b> (top body, not a govt organisation)", w=20),
  bx('pk', "<b>Why VOC (1602) not EIC (1600) = first joint-stock company:</b> in 1600 EIC ran a <b>per-VOYAGE</b> system (raise money from public, trade, share all profit, repeat); later it became proper, with <b>permanent capital</b>. A proper joint-stock company gives <b>dividends</b>, not all profit (profit pie = retain, re-invest, assets, dividends)."),
  sec("CHARTERS TO 1793: A STATE WITHIN A STATE", 'b'),
