  t("<b>Travancore before the SA</b>", "Built by <b>Marthanda Varma 29-58</b>: beat Dutch at <b>Colachel 1741</b>, centralised revenue State", "<b>Rama Varma 58-98</b> kept EIC alliance as hedge vs Mysore (Tipu's embargo on pepper) = trigger for <b>1789</b> attack = Cornwallis's pretext; died 1798, strain", w=20),
  tl(("1795", "<b>Treaty of Perpetual Friendship</b>: pay for British force vs Tipu"), ("1800", "<b>British Resident</b> at court (imprint of ToA 1765)"), ("1802", "Velu Thampi Dalawa PM (to 1809)"), ("1805", "<b>SA with Wellesley 98-05</b>, price of crushing revolt by <b>Nair troops</b> (unpaid salary); sovereignty lost on standard template"), ("Jan 1809", "<b>Kundara Proclamation</b>: Velu Thampi Dalawa, PM 1802-09, soldiers + peasants vs subsidy + interference (breach of non-interference); crushed within months, he died same year; Travancore subservient SA State")),
  bx('gr', "<b>Takeaway:</b> Travancore = worked example of how an SA is extracted (not at sword-point but for internal-security help the Resident may have destabilised). Every Ch 11 consequence (lost military jobs, high taxes, PoIR creeping in) played out in 4 years. Ch 7 has Marthanda Varma's monopoly + Colachel and Malabar 1766; Ch 11 lists Travancore as 8th signatory."),
  bx('ye', "<b>Wording:</b> Kundara = <b>'one of the most significant early revolts'</b> (text, slide: safer); handout flow chart says 'first organised revolt in south India'."),
